WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.000
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Every operations leader knows this feeling. The schedule says you have enough

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
people — but the phones are ringing off the hook. The client meeting is in two

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
weeks — and you're still writing the onboarding manual by hand. The top

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
performer just quit — and you didn't see it coming. For 28 years, Hatem Shalaby

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.000
lived these problems. Not as a consultant — as the person in the room when the

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
numbers didn't add up. He watched the same waste repeat itself, year after year.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:01:00.000
So he decided to build something different.

2
00:01:00.000 --> 00:02:00.000
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Helix Prime isn't another dashboard or a chatbot. It's a digital operations

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.000
team — four specialized roles that work together, around the clock. There's the

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.000
strategist — looking at the big picture, making sure every action aligns with

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.000
the business goal. The operations manager — watching the floor in real time,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:20.000
catching problems before they become crises. The talent director — connecting

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:24.000
the dots between who you need and who's available. And the learning coach —

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.000
turning every decision into a lesson that makes the whole team smarter. They

00:01:28.000 --> 00:02:00.000
don't just talk. They coordinate. They act. They learn.

3
00:02:00.000 --> 00:03:00.000
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Underneath, six engines handle the heavy lifting — the work that usually eats

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.000
up weeks of manager time. Staffing forecasts that tell you exactly how many

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.000
people you need, when — no more guessing. Real-time monitoring that flags

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:16.000
schedule problems before they hit your service levels. Client health tracking

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.000
that watches four key signals and warns you weeks before a client might leave.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.000
Onboarding automation that generates a complete operations plan in seconds — not

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.000
weeks. Talent pipeline management that links your forecasts to your hiring,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.000
automatically. And a CRM engine that keeps the sales pipeline and support work

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.000
in one place. And every result the system produces is recorded and traceable —

00:02:36.000 --> 00:03:00.000
so the team can see exactly what was decided and why.

4
00:03:00.000 --> 00:04:00.000
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.000
This is a working system — built and verified, step by step, in the open.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:08.000
Here's what the proof looks like: A test suite that runs against the real code —

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.000
automated, and growing. Every component built in the open, in a public

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.000
repository. No screenshots of things that don't run. No promises dressed up as

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.000
results. Engineers trust diagrams. Managers trust stories. But smart buyers

00:03:19.000 --> 00:04:00.000
trust working code you can run yourself.

5
00:04:00.000 --> 00:05:00.000
00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.000
Here's what makes Helix different from everything else out there. It works on

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.000
your laptop — no cloud required, no data leaving your building. It scales to the

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.000
cloud — when you're ready, there's a path. And it's built honestly: a public

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.000
alpha, with its real limits stated plainly in the README. This isn't about

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.000
replacing people. It's about giving your team the clarity and speed they've

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.000
always needed. Helix Prime. A digital operations team — built on real

00:04:23.000 --> 00:05:00.000
experience, built in the open. Experience. Engineering. Honesty.
